// `@linkName` fixes a C name someone else chose. A `type expose value` has one — its struct in the generated header —
// and so does a `type extern value` (the C header names its struct) —
// and an ordinary type has none: its C name is kama's to choose and never leaves the program.
@linkName("Config")
type value Settings { public int32 n; public ctor of(int32 n) { this.n = n; } }
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
